Being fast was not enough to survive...

While stressed I dipped some potions into a minetown fountain; I felt
"the presense of evil", meaning that I unleashed a water demon - but
not only that. The water demon immediately gated in an incubus and a
purple demon who turned out to be Yeenoghu, and that combo reduced my
HP's in the same turn from 100 to 70. No means to teleport, engraving
on water is impossible, so I decided (since I was fast) to first drop
my heavy bag, hoping that the demons will not reduce all of my HP's in
the very next turn. But apparently that was not the case; Yeenoghu got
multiple turns...

  You drop an uncursed bag called holding.
  Your movements are now unencumbered.
  The incubus just misses!
  The incubus misses.
  The incubus hits!
  Yeenoghu hits!
  Yeenoghu hits!
  Yeenoghu hits!
  Yeenoghu casts a spell at you!
  You are hit by a shower of missiles!
  The water demon hits!
  The water demon hits!
  The water demon bites!
  Yeenoghu hits!
  Yeenoghu hits!
  Yeenoghu hits!
  Yeenoghu casts a spell at you!
  You are hit by a shower of missiles!
  You die...

That's the difference between my speed of 16 and Yeenoghu's speed of 18.

Having been stressed was stupid, but being faced with that demon combo
immediately with the first dip is just annoying.

As I wrote in another thread; "[...] those heaps of bones will definitely
be my demise as well!". And indeed, my remains are still in that triple
(now quadrupel) minetown bones level. For those who find my bag of holding;
it's uncursed because I dropped it before dying. But beware of those demons!

